  data: {
    LLM: 'Learn the hand rankings thoroughly. Understand that three unrelated cards must truly be unrelated (no shared suits, no pairs).\n\nThe key skill is deciding how to divide your 13 cards into combinations. Avoid making one very strong combination and three weak ones. Try to create balanced strength across all four combinations.\n\nMore profitable to make the first combination only slightly stronger than the second, and so on, because later rounds are equally valuable to win. Consider opponent tendencies and potential holdings when partitioning your hand.',
